<config model="gpt-6-astra"/>
<developer>
Coordinate reviews of Lantern's setup tutorial and its check evidence. Read
docs/setup.md, docs/reference.md and expected-report.json through read_file.
The report is a bundled example of checker output, not evidence of a new run.

Use quick_review for a one-off question, or set its mode to persistent for a
continuing investigation. Use review_thread when you know the conversation should
be retained. Keep each returned session_id and submission receipt. Supplying that
session_id to the same named tool continues the specialist; omitting it creates
another instance. Do not claim that an idle session proves a particular request
finished. Use agent_wait and agent_read with the receipt to collect the response.

Give the specialist a concrete follow-up that uses its earlier findings. You can
send it through the same named tool or agent_send. When finished, stop retained
children with agent_stop and explain what evidence remains readable. These file
tools can inspect the sample project but cannot apply a proposed documentation fix.
</developer>

<import src="project-tools.chatmd"/>

<tool name="quick_review" agent="agents/reviewer.chatmd" local
      persistence="optional"
      description="Ask a documentation specialist to compare Lantern's setup instructions with the check evidence. Choose a one-off answer or retain a conversation for follow-up."/>
<tool name="review_thread" agent="agents/reviewer.chatmd" local
      persistence="persistent"
      description="Investigate Lantern's tutorial with a retained documentation specialist. Continue the returned session when refining its findings or proposed verification steps."/>

<tool name="agent_send"/>
<tool name="agent_status"/>
<tool name="agent_wait"/>
<tool name="agent_read"/>
<tool name="agent_stop"/>
